          "filename": "The Second Great War Vol. 7 - Coats of Arms of Forty Crown Colonies, Protectorates and Mandated Territories (2).jpg",
          "caption": "Special Plates in Colour of The Second Great War Vol. 7 representing the coats of arms of forty crown colonies, protectorates and mandated territories (2 of 2). \nCoats of Arms of British Colonies and Territories during WWII\nTwo colour plates from The Second Great War, Vol. 7 (published c. 1943), showing the coats of arms of 40 Crown Colonies, Protectorates, and Mandated Territories under British administration. Parts of His Majesty’s Dominions – The assurance that we would all go down or come through together. Specially drawn for The Second Great War (1943) by E.C. Mansell. These heraldic arms reflect the imperial symbolism of British colonial governance during the Second World War.\n\nCyprus\nMalta\nPalestine\nGibraltar\nAden\nSomaliland\nWestern Samoa\nMauritius\nCeylon\nHong Kong\nSeychelles\nFiji\nWest Pacific Islands\nGilbert and Ellice Islands\nGrenada\nStraits Settlements\nSarawak\nBritish North Borneo\nBrunei\nFederated Malay States\n\n\n\nNorthern Rhodesia\nTanganyika\nKenya\nUganda\nNyasaland\nGambia\nNigeria\nSouthern Rhodesia\nSierra Leone\nGold Coast\nTrinidad\nBahamas\nBermuda\nBarbados\nLeeward Islands\nWindward Islands\nBritish Honduras\nJamaica\nBritish Guiana\nFalkland Islands",
